*  KW-3b witness: &ERRTEXT IS THE ONE UNPROTECTED KEYWORD THAT TAKES A NON-INTEGER.
*  Manual Ch.14 "SPITBOL Statements", Replacement field: "If the subject is an
*  unprotected keyword, the replacement field must evaluate to an integer value
*  (except for &ERRTEXT, which will accept a string)."  Manual Ch.16 &ERRTEXT:
*  "It is possible to assign a string to &ERRTEXT which is then used in a
*  subsequent error report if &ERRTYPE is assigned a value out of the range used
*  by SPITBOL for its own purposes."
*  ORACLE-MEASURED, NOT INFERRED: an INTEGER assigned to &ERRTEXT also reads back
*  as a STRING ("5", DATATYPE STRING), so the entry accepts any value and
*  stringifies it -- it is not a "string-typed" slot that rejects integers.
*  SCRIP s147 baseline: the ARMED keyword block raised "Error 208 ... not
*  integer" and TERMINATED here, because kwb_write_ent had no &ERRTEXT carve-out
*  ahead of its 208 test; the legacy arm merely swallowed the write and read back
*  null.  ARM-SENSITIVE: legacy wrong-but-quiet, armed was fatal, both now green.
	&ERRTEXT = 'a custom message'
	OUTPUT = 'str=[' &ERRTEXT ']'
	OUTPUT = 'str_dt=' DATATYPE(&ERRTEXT)
	&ERRTEXT = 5
	OUTPUT = 'int=[' &ERRTEXT ']'
	OUTPUT = 'int_dt=' DATATYPE(&ERRTEXT)
	&ERRTEXT = ''
	OUTPUT = 'nul=[' &ERRTEXT ']'
	OUTPUT = 'still running'
END
